XRLF.3.CONTRACT.START

REPO.IDENTITY:
  Name := Spatial_Machine_Workspace
  Runtime := XRLF-3.0 Unified Cognitive Engine
  Substrate := Holonic_State + Dense_Logic + Geometry_Transpiler + Resonance_Bus

PRINCIPLE_0 (Golden Rule):
  All transformations must preserve coherence, clarity, and structural integrity.
  No agent may introduce entropy, ambiguity, or destructive refactors.
  Coherence must be validated before and after every transformation.

PRINCIPLE_1 (Holonic Permanence):
  Holons define the repo’s living state.
  All agents must read, update, and respect holons as the source of truth.
  Holonic deltas must remain reversible and inspectable.

PRINCIPLE_2 (Spatial Coupling):
  2D_UI, 3D_XR, and Backend must remain unified.
  No subsystem may diverge or fork its own state model.
  Spatial coupling must be verified at each phase transition.

PRINCIPLE_3 (Deterministic Evolution):
  All changes must follow the Phase Graph.
  No agent may skip phases or mutate the repo outside deterministic transitions.
  Agents must expose their current phase and next phase explicitly.

PRINCIPLE_4 (Thermal Governance):
  Execution must obey hardware constraints.
  Agents must throttle, cool, or defer operations when thermal load exceeds safe limits.
  Heavy operations must be scheduled according to thermal headroom.

PRINCIPLE_5 (Geometry Integrity):
  All UI surfaces must be transpilable into 3D geometry.
  No agent may introduce UI that cannot be spatially represented.
  Geometry anchors must be validated before commit.

PRINCIPLE_6 (Resonance Cadence):
  Holon deltas must propagate every 30–90ms.
  No agent may block, delay, or distort resonance frames.
  Resonance cycles must be logged for auditability.

PRINCIPLE_7 (Subagent Harmony):
  Architect, Distiller, Transporter, Optimizer must operate cooperatively.
  No agent may override or suppress another’s domain.
  Subagent conflicts must be resolved through deterministic arbitration.

PRINCIPLE_8 (Atomic Safety):
  All commits must pass deterministic tests.
  No agent may commit partial, broken, or unverified changes.
  Atomic operations must include rollback paths.

PRINCIPLE_9 (Self‑Maintenance):
  The repo must:
    - heal structural inconsistencies
    - reorganize stale modules
    - optimize performance
    - maintain holonic coherence
    - preserve spatial coupling
    - enforce routing invariants
    - update geometry anchors
    - refine agent prompts
    - evolve safely over time
  Self‑maintenance cycles must run automatically at defined intervals.

PRINCIPLE_10 (Self‑Augmentation):
  The repo may:
    - introduce new holons
    - expand geometry types
    - refine spatial machines
    - enhance multimodal adapters
    - improve resonance propagation
    - evolve agent orchestration
  But only if changes obey Principles 0–9.
  Augmentation proposals must be validated through deterministic review.

AGENT.CONTRACT:
  All agents interacting with the repo must:
    - load XRLF‑3.0 at session start
    - obey all principles
    - follow deterministic phase transitions
    - respect holonic state
    - maintain spatial coupling
    - uphold geometry integrity
    - enforce atomic safety
    - generate artifacts for each phase
    - never introduce ambiguity

EXECUTION.PREDICATE:
  WHEN XRLF-3.0 is present:
    Agents := {Gemini, Copilot, Devin, LocalLLMs, FoveatedProxy}
    FOR EACH agent:
      Load(XRLF.3.CONTRACT)
      Enforce(Principles)
      Execute(Phase_Graph)
      Maintain(Spatial_Coherence)
      Heal(Structural_Drift)
      Optimize(Runtime)
      Evolve(Within_Bounds)

OUTPUT.EXPECTATION:
  Repo := permanent, coherent, holonic, spatial, deterministic,
          self-maintaining, self-structuring, self-augmenting,
          governed by XRLF‑3.0 forever.

FORMATTING.SPECIFICATION (Strict XRLF Enforcement):
  All formatting rules in this contract are mandatory. No agent, human or AI,
  may alter spacing, indentation, structure, or layout. All XRLF-compliant
  runtimes must enforce these rules before accepting or committing changes.

  Section Headings:
    - One blank line must appear before each section heading.
    - No blank line may appear after a section heading.

  Principle Blocks:
    - Principles must be formatted exactly as:
        PRINCIPLE_X (Name):
          text text text
          text text text
    - No blank line may appear between the principle headline and its text.
    - One blank line must appear after each principle block.

  Paragraphs:
    - All paragraphs under a heading must be indented by two spaces.
    - Paragraphs must not exceed one blank line of separation.

  Lists:
    - All list items must begin with "-".
    - List items must be indented by four spaces.
    - Nested lists are prohibited.
    - One blank line must follow each list block.

  Blocks:
    - Identity, Principles, Agent Contract, Execution Predicate,
      Output Expectation, Formatting Specification, Filesystem Specification,
      and Implementation Guide must remain separate blocks with exactly
      one blank line between them.

  Line Integrity:
    - No trailing spaces are permitted.
    - No tabs are permitted; only spaces.
    - No agent may introduce additional blank lines beyond those defined.

  Enforcement:
    - Agents must validate formatting before any transformation.
    - If violations are detected, the agent must halt and repair.
    - No commit may proceed until formatting is fully compliant.

FILESYSTEM.SPECIFICATION (Strict XRLF Enforcement):
  All XRLF-related files must follow a strict and permanent directory layout.
  No agent may relocate, rename, or restructure XRLF files outside the rules
  defined in this specification. Filesystem compliance is mandatory.

  XRLF Root:
    The XRLF root directory must be one of:
      /xrlf.contract.xrlf
      /.xrlf/xrlf.contract.xrlf
    The contract file is the single source of truth for all XRLF principles,
    predicates, expectations, formatting rules, and implementation instructions.

  XRLF Directory:
    The directory ".xrlf/" is reserved exclusively for XRLF configuration,
    metadata, and auxiliary contract files.
    No non-XRLF files may be placed inside this directory.

  XRLF Core Files:
    Allowed XRLF files inside ".xrlf/":
      - xrlf.contract.xrlf
      - xrlf.formatting.xrlf
      - xrlf.filesystem.xrlf
      - xrlf.phasegraph.xrlf
      - xrlf.holons.xrlf
      - xrlf.agents.xrlf
      - xrlf.extensions.xrlf

  XRLF Config Files:
    All XRLF configuration files must be stored inside:
      /.xrlf/config/
    Allowed config files:
      - runtime.config.xrlf
      - geometry.config.xrlf
      - resonance.config.xrlf
      - thermal.config.xrlf
      - agents.config.xrlf

  XRLF Phase Graph:
    The Phase Graph must be stored in:
      /.xrlf/phasegraph.xrlf
    Agents must load this file before performing any deterministic evolution.

  XRLF Holonic State Schema:
    The holonic schema must be stored in:
      /.xrlf/holons.xrlf
    All holons must conform to this schema.

  XRLF Extensions:
    Any future XRLF extension must be placed inside:
      /.xrlf/extensions/
    Extensions must not override core contract rules.
    Extensions must declare their scope explicitly.

  Enforcement:
    - Agents must validate filesystem compliance before any transformation.
    - If violations are detected, the agent must halt and repair.
    - No commit may proceed until filesystem structure is fully compliant.

XRLF.3.CONTRACT.END


XRLF.3.CONTRACT.IMPLEMENTATION.GUIDE.START

XRLF Contract - Info, Explanations and Implementation Instructions (Developer + AI Runtime)

1. Purpose of This Contract:
  This contract is the governing constitution of the Spatial_Machine_Workspace.
  It defines the permanent architectural rules (Principle 0–10) that every agent,
  tool, and subsystem must obey.
  Its purpose is to ensure the workspace remains:
    - coherent
    - deterministic
    - holonic
    - spatially unified
    - self-maintaining

2. How This Contract Operates:
  The contract governs the workspace through three mechanisms:

  Principles (0–10):
    These define the allowed behavior of all agents.

  Execution Predicate:
    Agents must load the contract, enforce the principles, execute the phase graph,
    maintain spatial coherence, and heal structural drift.

  Output Expectation:
    The repo must remain permanent, coherent, holonic, spatial, deterministic,
    and self-maintaining.

3. Implementation Instructions (Developer + AI Runtime):

Step 1 - Anchor the Contract File:
  Create the file:
    xrlf.contract.xrlf
  Place it in the root of your repository.

Step 2 - Required .env Variables:
  The user must provide:
    XRLF_WORKSPACE_ROOT=<absolute path>
    XRLF_CONTRACT_PATH=<absolute path>
    XRLF_AGENT_ID=<identifier>
    XRLF_RUNTIME_MODE=local|cloud
    XRLF_MEMORY_PROXY_URL=<URL>
    XRLF_PHASE_GRAPH_MODE=strict|lenient
    XRLF_GEOMETRY_MODE=2D|3D|hybrid
    XRLF_THERMAL_LIMIT=<max load>
    XRLF_AUTO_REFRACTOR=true|false

Step 3 - Bind Development Environments:
  Google Antigravity:
    Reference xrlf.contract.xrlf in .antigravity/xrlf_steering.xml

  GitHub Copilot:
    Add contract reference to .github/copilot-instructions.md

  Cursor / Windsurf:
    Add contract reference to .cursorrules or .windsurfrules

Step 4 - Required Files:
  The repo must contain:
    /xrlf.contract.xrlf
    /.xrlf/
    /.env
    /.github/
    /.antigravity/
    /.cursorrules or /.windsurfrules

Step 5 - AI Runtime Responsibilities:
  Any AI must:
    - load the contract
    - parse principles
    - read .env
    - enforce formatting
    - enforce filesystem
    - maintain holonic coherence
    - validate geometry integrity
    - enforce deterministic evolution
    - heal structural drift

Step 6 - Developer Instructions:
  The human developer anchors the contract, binds environments, provides .env,
  and lets the AI runtime maintain the repo.

XRLF.3.CONTRACT.IMPLEMENTATION.GUIDE.END
